Rāma shoots one shaft through seven sālas --- Shaft pierces hill and earth and regains quiver --- Sugrīva bows and hails Rāma god-slaying strength --- Sugrīva demands Vālin death now --- Rāma hides party and sends Sugrīva roaring --- Brothers exchange thunderous fist blows --- Rāma withholds arrow confusing identical twins --- Sugrīva flees wounded to R̥śyamūka as Vālin turns back --- Sugrīva reproaches Rāma for betrayal --- Rāma blames twin likeness and Lakṣmaṇa garlands Sugrīva